      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gove_City%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after Grenville Gove, a 19th‑century Kansas cavalry officer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gove_City%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "It became the county seat of Gove County in 1886 and was officially incorporated two years later.",
